  "fixture": "Benchmarks/Fixtures/FrontendPair.ix",
  "source": "namespace Demo\n\nstructure Pair (α : Type) : Type where\n  fst : α\n  snd : α\n\ntheorem swap_fst {α : Type} (a b : α) :\n    Eq (swap (Pair.mk a b)).fst b := by\n  rfl\n\ndef swap {α : Type} (p : Pair α) : Pair α :=\n  let x := p.fst;\n  { fst := p.snd, snd := x }\n\ndef keep {α : Type} (!1 x : α) : ! α := x\n\nend Demo\n",
  "source_bytes": 319,
  "implementation": "Benchmarks/FrontendRaw.lean",
  "commands": [
    "lake build bench-frontend-eval",
    "lake env .lake/build/bin/bench-frontend-eval raw 3 --prove"
  ],
  "method": "Generic Rust Aiur bytecode execution of direct constrained parsing and elaboration. Public input is the source Blake3 digest; private IO contains the source bytes, range-checked and hash-verified in Aiur. Boolean result checks expected core types/bodies/contracts. No Lean frontend evaluation or Claim.eval in this path.",
  "supported_subset": [
    "One namespace and one initial homogeneous record with one explicit Type parameter and any positive number of fields.",
    "ASCII and basic Greek identifiers; whitespace; grouped explicit and implicit declaration binders.",
    "Definitions and theorems; acyclic forward references resolved through on-demand elaboration.",
    "Application, inferred let types, record literals with fields in arbitrary order, named field projections, implicit constructor type parameter.",
    "A leading implicit Type argument solved from the first explicit argument, using variable/record-type patterns.",
    "Eq and by rfl, with definition unfolding, beta, let and constructor-projection reduction.",
    "Unique and linear/unique binder flags and unique-result metadata."
  ],
  "scope_limits": [
    "This is a subset implementation, not a port of Ix.Frontend or a drop-in replacement.",
    "Uses a custom de Bruijn core with dedicated record, Eq and contract nodes. Does not serialize an Ix environment or Ixon.",
    "Does not seed the 115 prelude constants or generate constructor/projection/recursor declarations; record operations are represented directly. Unlike the baseline it does not check presence of generated recursor members.",
    "No general metavariable solver, universe-polymorphic declarations, recursive definitions, comments, imports, macros, typeclasses or general tactics.",
    "One implicit Type argument inferred from variable/record-type patterns; not general dependent elaboration.",
    "Reduction depth bounded by 512 and declaration dependency recursion bounded by declaration count.",
    "Preserves resource annotations but does not run the separate resource checker, as with the baseline.",
    "Neither implementation has a formal equivalence proof; differential tests cover the listed cases only."
  ],
  "measurement_notes": [
    "Execution medians of three runs after validation warm-up; each execute call has its own trace/memo table.",
    "Compilation, Aiur system construction, input digest/witness preparation, validation, and proof generation are excluded from execution timing.",
    "One end-to-end proof/verification sample; default repository commitment/FRI parameters.",
    "Rows are dynamic function/memory unique rows; FFT costs are unpadded repository estimates, not measured proving time.",
    "Total FFT includes fixed Bytes1/Bytes2 cost of 107333632. Dynamic FFT excludes both.",
    "Ratios compare the same 319-byte fixture but different frontend scope and claim interfaces. They are not measured speedups for a complete frontend replacement.",
    "Saved IxVM baseline has one execution sample and no proof; raw has three execution samples and one proof."
  ],
